WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.890
- Today on Drew,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.310
we wrap up our look back at season one.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.760
Our first kiss and it was not onscreen.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.570
- I remember that.
(Drew laughs)

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.440
- [Announcer] It all starts Monday.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.840
The Drew Barrymore Show
is on location from LA.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.728
Hollywood's biggest stars
and big hometown surprises.

00:00:21.728 --> 00:00:22.561
(Drew yells)

00:00:22.561 --> 00:00:24.200
- Oh my God, we have to stop.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.609
It all starts now.
(audience applauds)

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:30.670
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:33.163
- [Announcer] Please
welcome Drew Barrymore.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.620
- Hi, everyone, I can't
believe that season two

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.120
of The Drew Barrymore Show

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.680
starts this Monday, September 13th.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.360
And we're so excited that we decided

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.550
to make it a two week premiere event,

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.580
celebrating hometowns and that feeling

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.750
that there is no place like home.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.930
And next week, we're kicking
off the season in my hometown

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.980
of Los Angeles and then
we're headed back here

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.880
to my new hometown of New York.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.480
But we wanna celebrate
your hometown as well.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.160
So write into TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.890
and tell us why your
hometown is special to you.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.510
Today, we're wrapping up
a week-long celebration

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.970
of our favorite moments from season one.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:21.680
And we have a very special surprise

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.850
for an incredible Drew Gooder.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.180
Her name is Alicia White

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.360
and she was born and raised in Queens.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.440
And after seeing the neglect
of parks and outdoor spaces

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.750
in her area, she created Project Petals,

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.410
a nonprofit focused on
revitalization and development

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.510
of underserved communities.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:45.450
Alicia is backstage right
now with her sister, Tiffany.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.450
And guess what?

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.660
They think they're here to
get a tour of the studio.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:53.320
They have no idea we're filming
right now and at the end

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.730
of the show, we're gonna surprise them.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.140
Guess what with?

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.260
Well, you're gonna have to find out.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.820
Right now, let's dive into
more memorable moments

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.250
from last season.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.470
First up is a guest I was
honored to share scenes with.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:11.460
Oh, Hugh Grant, otherwise known as Hubert,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.540
is someone I just love so much.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.380
And he stopped in and
we covered everything

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:20.810
from our first conversation
to our first kiss

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:23.350
and it was not onscreen.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:24.923
Uh-huh, watch this.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.803
Let's start on how we first met.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.113
Do you remember?

00:02:35.847 --> 00:02:37.730
(Drew laughs)

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.763
We actually didn't meet in person.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.370
I reached out to you.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.181
- Oh my God, you did!

00:02:45.181 --> 00:02:46.510
You were so nice.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:49.120
You were so nice, yes.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.350
It was during the dark days
of my Divine Brown scandal.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.908
I was just an idiot.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.560
(Drew laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.740
I was a grown up idiot who
got caught by the police.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.560
And I was back in England with
5,000 members of the press

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.163
around the borders of my farm.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.014
And I opened a letter from you

00:03:12.014 --> 00:03:14.430
that was very supportive and nice.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.950
And it was very cheering up.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.020
And I thought I love Drew Barrymore.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:25.020
Words of support from an actress
I didn't know in Hollywood

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.280
was lovely, so you'll always
have a place in my heart.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.150
- Oh, I loved you so much.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.960
That whole incident just
I related in my own life

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.360
and I think that whether
it's an actor or a politician

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:45.360
or anything in between, we
expect people to be infallible,

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.530
perfect, never flawed.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.320
And God forbid we do anything
in our personal lives

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.530
that we would like to remain personal,

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:59.240
but we don't have that
privilege at a certain point

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.850
because the cat gets let out of the bag

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.680
and I just had to reach out to you.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.260
I just appreciated you and I was so...

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.266
I mean, and you were just
the most charming human.

00:04:11.266 --> 00:04:14.280
I loved getting to know you

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.200
on our movie, "Music and Lyrics".

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.880
And it's just one of
my very favorite movies

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.990
and it makes me so happy.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.679
It was a good movie, it was a happy movie.

00:04:23.679 --> 00:04:25.723
- I agree with you

00:04:25.723 --> 00:04:27.534
'cause I love to hate
the films I've been in.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:28.972
And I do hate some of them.
(audience laughs)

00:04:28.972 --> 00:04:33.005
But "Music and Lyrics",
it's impossible to hate.

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:34.930
We're so good in it

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:35.780
and so charming.
(audience laughs)

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:38.340
- If you think I'm good in
it, that means a lot to me

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.220
because I have the
deepest respect for you.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.420
Beyond your charm and your heart,

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.630
your talent is just unparalleled.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.750
And you've had a long body of work,

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:52.860
so you shan't argue me
out of that hypothesis.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.470
- But it wasn't, but Drew,
I think that film works

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.490
maybe we acted quite well,

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.040
but here's the weird thing.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.040
We had chemistry and there
were people I remember

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.457
before we shot that,
"It's a bit disgusting

00:05:05.457 --> 00:05:08.310
"'cause he's 180 and she's like 20."

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:12.710
But actually, we had a bit of chemistry.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.040
- We really did.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.530
And it was funny too
because when Hugh and I met,

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:21.570
Hugh, you can be a bit of a
curmudgeon from time to time

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.616
(audience laughs)

00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:28.510
and I of course am like a
Labrador in heat and (Drew pants)

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.220
I'm so excited with joy.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.040
And so when we both met, we were like,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.793
oh, we're kind of different people.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.840
- That is absolutely true.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.040
- It was.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.356
- Maybe that's why it
had a bit of crackle.

00:05:40.356 --> 00:05:43.250
- And then we really
got to know each other

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.240
and accept each other for who we were

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.610
and it became easy.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.800
And then we just used
to sit around and laugh.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.000
That being said, one of the moments

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.610
that I had some of the most moxie,

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:57.070
and I don't think we've
ever talked about this,

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:02.040
I walked into I think it
was like the Waverly Inn

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.296
and this was years ago
and I'd had a few drinks.

00:06:06.296 --> 00:06:08.480
(Drew laughs)

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.370
And I walked in and I ran into you.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:13.550
And instead of saying hello,
I grabbed you by the collar

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.880
and I fully started kissing you.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.560
- Yes.
(audience laughs)

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.237
I remember that.

00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:23.020
(audience laughs)

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:27.330
- Can I do you of what I saw?

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.163
- Yes, yes, please.

00:06:28.163 --> 00:06:28.996
- You went...

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.770
- [Hugh] I don't think that's true.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:34.110
- But you were like, oh.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.979
The expression was you've never
greeted me that way before.

00:06:37.979 --> 00:06:40.610
And then you were like
had a second thought

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.250
and you were like, you
know I'm not hating this.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:48.250
And then we flirted and then
it was like we were like,

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.133
okay, yeah, bye, see you soon.

00:06:52.128 --> 00:06:53.860
- It was really bizarre.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:55.017
I was very drunk as well.

00:06:55.017 --> 00:06:57.640
And I was with some very nice

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.343
but not drunk studio executives from LA.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.280
And they were very surprised.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.890
Someone said, "Oh,
there's Drew Barrymore."

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:07.770
I get up to say hi and then
we make out for 10 minutes.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.390
And then I sit down again and
I'm talking about the script.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:13.160
- Well, I guess we've grown up a bit.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.083
Do you think growing up
is overrated, Hubert?

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.874
- Yeah, I hate responsibility.

00:07:20.874 --> 00:07:22.800
I don't want this.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.780
I'm looking after five
children and an elderly father

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.960
and I don't like it.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.640
I keep looking around
for someone more grown up

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.460
to come and do it for me.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.350
It's awful.

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:37.760
- And yet, the last time we
talked, the way that you talk

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.370
about the way you look at life now,

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:45.370
having five children's eyes
to look through, look after

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:50.187
and look into, you seem very changed.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.510
- I'm simultaneously utterly
exhausted and miserable

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.644
and I'm clearly the
happiest I've ever been.

00:08:00.644 --> 00:08:02.570
I see that now.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:03.600
It's so nice.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.840
All those cliches are true.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.910
All that love is just so nice.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.580
- I think that--

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:11.000
- Not just the children,
but the wife as well.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.123
I have a top wife.

00:08:13.174 --> 00:08:16.022
You must meet her, she's terrifying.

00:08:16.022 --> 00:08:17.840
(audience laughs)

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:21.438
Swedish, much more
manly than me in terms--

00:08:21.438 --> 00:08:24.390
(Drew laughs)

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:28.118
But really cool and now you see I'm happy.

00:08:28.118 --> 00:08:29.460
(audience applauds)

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.990
- Oh, Hugh, I just...
(Drew swoons)

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.610
You're the best.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.960
More memories with Hubert when we return.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.426
Don't go anywhere.

00:08:38.426 --> 00:08:41.009
(upbeat music)

00:08:44.295 --> 00:08:46.370
I want juice, dirt.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:47.690
I wanna pull back the curtain

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.570
on some of your most iconic roles.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:53.660
- Rene was a genius at
being British Bridget.

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.420
But I do remember that she came in

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.780
for the first read through

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:59.723
and she sounded very, very posh.

00:08:59.723 --> 00:09:01.824
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

00:09:01.824 --> 00:09:04.407
(upbeat music)

00:09:07.215 --> 00:09:09.798
(upbeat music)

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:12.030
- Welcome back.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.110
All week long, we're bringing you some

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:17.790
of our favorite stand out
moments from season one

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.150
with some director's cut
commentary sprinkled in.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.750
And when Hugh Grant came on the show,

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.910
he revealed some director's
cut commentary of his own.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.000
We asked him to pull back the curtain

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.120
on some of his most famous films

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.160
in something we call Behind the Scenes

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.900
and he did not hold back.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.250
Take a look.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.540
I wanna pull back the curtain

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.300
on some of your most iconic
roles in something we like

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.346
to call Behind the Scenes.

00:09:45.346 --> 00:09:48.590
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:53.420
Okay, I want juice, dirt,
fly on the wall, anything

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:57.850
that comes to mind when I
mention these movies if you will,

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.310
please and thank you.

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:02.530
Let's start with "Notting Hill".

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.040
- [Hugh] There's so much.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.990
- [Drew] Oh, give it to me, Hubert.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.690
- Remember the scene with the brownies

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.020
when everyone's sitting
around having dinner

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.860
and it's about who's gonna
eat the last brownie?

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.010
- Yes.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:16.760
- Hugh Bonneville who Americans
think is a classy actor,

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.650
what he got up to during that scene

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:21.930
deliberately putting brownies on my chair

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.694
so that I would sit on
them in my white trousers

00:10:24.694 --> 00:10:27.660
and then they could all laugh at my bum

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.510
in between takes.

00:10:29.622 --> 00:10:30.883
I remember that.

00:10:31.882 --> 00:10:35.000
- Okay, "Four Weddings and a Funeral".

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.180
- Well, yeah, panic.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.270
I remember the director, he
really, 'cause we had no money,

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:42.500
we made that film for a
minuscule amount of money

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.380
and in 36 days.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:46.830
And he just lost it all the time.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.810
He would throw his cup
of tea against the wall

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:53.126
and say, "(bleeping) I
can't make this film!"

00:10:53.126 --> 00:10:55.573
(Drew laughs)

00:10:55.573 --> 00:10:56.650
And we said, but you have to,

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.480
you've gotta shoot
another whole scene here.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.437
It's two pages and he'd say,

00:11:00.437 --> 00:11:02.670
"Oh, but there's five
minutes left in the day."

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:03.690
And so he'd say, "Stand
against that wall."

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:06.650
It was like we'd just
stand there in a line

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:08.840
and we'd just be the line
with one camera on us

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.930
and that is there is a
scene in the film like that,

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.014
took seven minutes to shoot.

00:11:14.014 --> 00:11:16.404
(audience laughs)

00:11:16.404 --> 00:11:17.972
(Drew laughs)

00:11:17.972 --> 00:11:20.240
- Okay, I'm so glad I asked.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.974
Okay, "About a Boy".

00:11:22.974 --> 00:11:27.040
- "About a Boy", he's a big star now,

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.900
not that baby, but the boy.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:29.980
(Drew laughs)

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:33.310
- Nicholas Hoult, by
the way, and he's hot.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:34.930
- [Hugh] Yes, yes and we chose him

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:37.650
because he was such a nerd and a geek.

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:41.202
- I know, I mean, with all due respect,

00:11:41.202 --> 00:11:45.780
he's posed as a real outsider boy

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.850
and he grew up to be really hot.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.130
- Yes, yes, he did.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:55.130
- Okay, "Bridget Jones Diary".

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:58.970
- Well, there you have
Rene who was a genius

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:04.240
at being British Bridget, but
I do remember that she went

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.920
through some interesting phases on the way

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.563
to getting that British
accent during rehearsals.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:12.580
She came in for the first read through

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.420
and she sounded like Princess Margaret,

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.697
very, very posh and grand.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:22.700
And then the next time she came in,

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.650
someone had told her obviously

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.600
that maybe bring it down a bit.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:29.535
But then she sounded a bit
like she'd had a stroke.

00:12:29.535 --> 00:12:31.610
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:33.553
And then she absolutely nailed it.

00:12:34.445 --> 00:12:36.060
It's an absolute triumph.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:38.520
And of course, she did
that accent not just

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.670
in the performance but between
takes and she never reverted

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.310
to American until the wrap party

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:47.370
when that was the first time
I'd ever heard her speak

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.460
with her Texan accent

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:51.875
and I quite honestly
found it unconvincing.

00:12:51.875 --> 00:12:53.540
(audience laughs)

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:57.740
- I love that detail and
I love hearing that intel

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:58.670
of her process.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.700
Great, thank you so much.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:03.417
Okay, "Mickey Blue Eyes".

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:09.800
- Oh, well, that's Jimmy Caan
and what can I tell you about?

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.370
Well, I can tell you that
with my then-girlfriend,

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:15.370
Elizabeth Hurley produced the film

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:20.370
and we had a lot of let's call
them specialists or advisors

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:24.440
on the set who knew all
about the New York mob.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:25.540
Let's just say that.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.240
And she was brilliant with them.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.400
If we needed anything done,
she would flirt with one

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:34.990
of these guys and she'd go
and sit on one of their knees

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:37.460
and compare their manicures.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:38.997
And say, "Oh, no, you've
got such lovely jewelry

00:13:38.997 --> 00:13:40.460
"and such lovely nails."

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:41.910
And they'd do anything for us.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:44.550
We know if we had a problem
with planes going overhead

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.360
ruining the soundtrack, one
of them would get on the phone

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:50.170
and suddenly, JFK had
redirected all the planes

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:52.770
from that particular part of Manhattan.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.990
- Oh my God, I love that story.

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.890
I'll never forget you and her stepping out

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.510
and she was in that
Versace safety pin dress.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:03.230
You know there are
iconic moments in fashion

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:04.670
and that will always be one,

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:07.430
that evening you two stepped out.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:11.010
- Well, yeah, it ended up that
way, but it was a pure fluke.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:14.830
We were unsuccessful actors.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.330
Well, we weren't that unsuccessful

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.000
but we were not well known in any way.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.710
And suddenly this big premiere
comes along for this film

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.360
and she has nothing to wear.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.820
And I think I said, I
think you can borrow stuff.

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:28.510
I think that's what people do.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.650
The big designers will lend you something.

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:31.650
And so we rang around.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:33.320
We didn't have an assistant or a publicist

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:34.153
or anything like that.

00:14:34.153 --> 00:14:36.270
We plucked up our courage, rang around

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.690
and they all said, "No, who are you?"

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:38.907
And then Versace said,

00:14:38.907 --> 00:14:41.410
"Yes, we got something
but only one thing."

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:42.243
And they sent it round

00:14:42.243 --> 00:14:44.580
and it was this was the
one dress that arrived.

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:45.770
And she put it on

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:49.389
and I remember being
slightly startled by it.

00:14:49.389 --> 00:14:51.576
(Hugh laughs)
- [Drew] Oh, I bet you were.

00:14:51.576 --> 00:14:52.683
- [Hugh] Hot.

00:14:52.683 --> 00:14:54.960
Anyway, and then the rest is history.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.274
It became a thing.

00:14:56.274 --> 00:14:57.720
(audience applauds)

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.400
- Elizabeth Hurley's safety pin dress,

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.170
yeah, that's always going to be iconic.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.520
All right, our season two
pre-party is just getting started

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.930
and we will be right back

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:10.290
with more season one
memorable moments in a minute.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.713
Don't move.

00:15:11.713 --> 00:15:14.296
(upbeat music)

00:15:20.016 --> 00:15:21.190
(upbeat music)

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:23.670
The internet moves so
fast I can barely keep up.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.770
Luckily, our team combs
through it every day

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.759
bringing us jewels like this.

00:15:27.759 --> 00:15:28.935
- Hi, Drew.

00:15:28.935 --> 00:15:30.802
I'm Autumna California Bailey.

00:15:30.802 --> 00:15:34.099
I love skating, watch me!

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:36.599
(light music)

00:15:51.203 --> 00:15:53.750
- That was a real gem.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:54.923
Thanks, internet.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.363
(upbeat music)

00:16:02.978 --> 00:16:05.600
(upbeat music)

