Welcome back.

00:16:06.433 --> 00:16:08.950
We're checking out some
of our favorite moments

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.220
from season one to get geared up

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:15.760
for our big season two premiere
this Monday, September 13th.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.250
Next up is a segment
where I got to eat dessert

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.520
while chatting with adorable kids.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.720
It doesn't get much better than that.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:26.580
Joshua, Isaiah, Caleb and
Micah are better known

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.600
as the Yummy Brothers.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:30.300
They're kid entrepreneurs

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:34.250
who turned their family cookie
recipes into a business.

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.777
And we had a surprise for them

00:16:35.777 --> 00:16:38.130
and it turned out they had one for us too.

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:40.670
And anyway, watch this.

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:43.540
How did you guys get
into the cookie business?

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.360
- First, we went to go ask our mom

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:47.792
would she approve of the business.

00:16:47.792 --> 00:16:50.860
Then she told us to go
sit down with our dad.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.730
And our dad eventually he agreed to do it

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:55.970
and we came up with the name and the logo

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.980
and it went off from there.

00:16:57.980 --> 00:17:01.360
- Joshua, what has it been
like working with your brothers

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.130
and starting a business?

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:06.253
- Well, it has been really
fun to be able to work

00:17:06.253 --> 00:17:08.640
with brothers, my mom and my dad.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.730
And another thing that I really love is

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:14.050
that we're inspiring kids
and adults across the world

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.050
to be entrepreneurs.

00:17:16.033 --> 00:17:19.020
(audience applauds)
- I mean, that's so wise.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:21.630
Micah, you guys are going to school

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:23.880
and running a successful business.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.340
How are you managing it all?

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:31.006
- Well, how we're doing this
is we do our schoolwork first

00:17:31.006 --> 00:17:33.129
and then we bake the cookies.

00:17:33.129 --> 00:17:35.947
(audience laughs)

00:17:35.947 --> 00:17:38.953
- Caleb, what are you gonna do
with the money you're making?

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:42.610
- Well, actually we
created another business

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:46.480
called Kidpreneur Expo
which is an online platform

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:50.150
that allows kidpreneurs that advertise

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:52.170
and market in their business.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.727
(audience applauds)

00:17:53.727 --> 00:17:56.010
- That's really smart.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.040
I learned early that marketing

00:17:58.040 --> 00:17:59.820
and advertising is very important

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:02.790
because it's how you tell your story.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.390
And it's a great way
for you to take control

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:09.350
but also make sure it's
exactly the way you see it.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:12.360
Isaiah, you are all such cool dudes.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.940
What would you tell someone

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:18.030
who thought baking was a girl thing?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:21.140
- Well, Drew, that's an awesome question.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.110
Let's say in my trip of imagination

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:27.080
you're on a Saturday
morning having some coffee,

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.980
probably just relaxing and
you have your cookies baking

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:33.360
in the oven at 350 degrees.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.530
Then when they get out, you take a bite

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:38.533
and ooey gooey chocolate
all over your mouth.

00:18:40.816 --> 00:18:42.187
- [Isaiah] And another thing, Drew.

00:18:42.187 --> 00:18:43.020
- [Drew] Yeah.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.430
One of our biggest supporters
was our grandfather.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:49.180
And he would always tell us
whatever you put your mind to

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.780
you can always do it.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:54.770
- I am so excited to
be talking to you guys.

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:59.260
And I know that you sent us
some of your yummy cookies.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:01.530
Okay, yum, yum, yum, yum, yum.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:02.670
What do we have?

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:04.450
Walk me through it, gentlemen.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:07.690
- All right, so we have the two face

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:10.868
which is double dark chocolate
mixed with chocolate chip.

00:19:10.868 --> 00:19:15.770
Then we have chocolate
chip, snickerdoodle.

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:18.650
Then there's cookies and cream,

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:21.020
Papa's white chocolate macadamia nut

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.960
that was named after our grandfather

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:26.460
because he loved macadamia nuts,

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:28.756
and then oatmeal.

00:19:28.756 --> 00:19:32.839
- [Drew] Mm-mm.
(audience laughs)

00:19:34.033 --> 00:19:35.650
- Cookies that we picked out for you

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:40.650
is Drew's ET cookie,
which means extra tasty.

00:19:43.573 --> 00:19:47.602
- Oh, I love it!
(audience applauds)

00:19:47.602 --> 00:19:52.602
Oh, gosh, you gentlemen are
so handsome and so talented.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.580
Oh my gosh.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.660
- [Isaiah] In the Drew's cookie,

00:19:56.660 --> 00:20:00.140
there's pecans, toffee and chocolate chip.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:02.180
- I must tell you guys

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.220
these are truly some of the
best cookies I've ever had

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.320
in my life and I'm not just saying that.

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.840
These are perfect.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:14.190
Their texture is exactly what you dream of

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:16.100
and there are so many different flavors

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.320
from all the different nuts.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.570
They're incredible.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:22.820
You guys have made an
extraordinary product.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.650
And I know that one of your goals is

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:27.540
to sell your cookies nationwide.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:32.540
And I actually heard that you
would love to sell in a store

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:37.430
and I reached out to the
owners of Slim and Husky's,

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:42.280
the first black-owned pizza
franchise in the country.

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:43.490
- Awesome!
- We love that place.

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:45.650
We go there all the time.

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:47.060
Their food is great.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:51.610
- Their successful pizza
empire has stores nationwide.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:55.590
And I would love to welcome
in the wonderful co-owners

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:59.961
of Slim and Husky's,
Clint, EJ and Derrick.

00:20:59.961 --> 00:21:02.365
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

00:21:02.365 --> 00:21:04.816
- How are y'all doing?

00:21:04.816 --> 00:21:05.649
- What's up, fellas?

00:21:05.649 --> 00:21:07.580
- Man, it's great to meet you guys.

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.730
We wanted to hop on
and say congratulations

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:11.320
on all you guys' success.

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:13.700
You guys are true leaders
for your communities

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:14.650
and your families.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.680
I just wanna tell you to keep on going.

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:19.337
The best is yet to come for you guys.

00:21:19.337 --> 00:21:20.170
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:22.890
- Man, we just want you
guys to know if you focus,

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:25.930
continue doing what you love
with the people that you love,

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.270
man, you can't go wrong.

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:30.570
So much success to you guys.

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:32.440
- What we're going to do is allow you guys

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.650
to sell your cookies
in our Atlanta stores.

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:35.796
How does that sound?

00:21:35.796 --> 00:21:37.810
(audience applauds)

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.460
- Let's go!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:40.500
- Awesome, awesome.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.780
So what we'll do, we'll work together

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:42.860
on a marketing strategy

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:44.300
and we'll figure out
how to make it all work.

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.460
That sound good?

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:47.010
- Yeah, great.
- [EJ] Awesome.

00:21:48.319 --> 00:21:50.360
- Thank you for having us here.

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:53.380
- We're obviously if we could
be so lucky to have each

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:54.990
and every one of you up on our website.

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:57.230
It's TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com
shining lights

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:58.500
on your businesses.

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:00.270
We love all of you

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:01.860
and everything that you're doing

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:03.480
in your business communities,

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:07.073
as well as being really smart businessmen.

00:22:08.024 --> 00:22:10.000
- Thank you so much.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:13.290
But Drew, you know what would be good?

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:18.046
If we did an exclusive Slim
and Husky's special cookie.

00:22:18.046 --> 00:22:20.315
(audience applauds)

00:22:20.315 --> 00:22:21.154
- We like that.

00:22:21.154 --> 00:22:22.754
- [Clint] We love it.

00:22:22.754 --> 00:22:24.290
- [Derrick] Let's make it happen.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:27.130
- How impressive are those boys?

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:30.250
The best, and since we last saw them,

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:33.850
the Yummy Brothers marked
a special milestone.

00:22:33.850 --> 00:22:37.880
They welcomed another brother
into the family business.

00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:40.890
Baby Andrew is now the
fifth Yummy Brother.

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:44.520
And we hear he's been assigned
to the very important task

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:47.290
of taste-testing the cookies.

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:49.660
We wish them all the very best.

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:51.580
Now, we have to take a quick
break, so I'm gonna go see

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:53.640
if we have any leftover
cookies in our kitchen.

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:56.930
So we'll be right back with
more season one memories

00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:58.883
and fun facts.

00:22:58.883 --> 00:23:01.466
(upbeat music)

00:23:07.138 --> 00:23:09.910
(upbeat music)

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:12.880
Welcome back to our season two pre-party

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:13.940
and we're checking out some

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:15.650
of our favorite season one moments.

00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:19.300
And I'm throwing in a little
behind the scenes commentary,

00:23:19.300 --> 00:23:22.020
stuff you wouldn't have seen before.

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:25.310
I am truly obsessed with this next guess.

00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:29.660
All season long, I was vision boarding

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:33.140
and trying to manifest that
she would come on the show.

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:37.010
And finally, my dream actually came true.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:41.050
And her appearance truly sparked joy.

00:23:41.050 --> 00:23:42.771
This is our conversation

00:23:42.771 --> 00:23:46.390
with the declutter queen, Marie Kondo.

00:23:46.390 --> 00:23:47.900
Take a look.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:50.040
I have a question, Marie,

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:52.380
when I first discovered Marie Kondo,

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:54.460
I was basically a hoarder.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:57.910
I had 15 layers to everything.

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:02.390
The chair had a pillow
and a throw blanket.

00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:07.390
And I wonder when you
do start to take away

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:14.550
and go layer by layer and
get to a more sane place,

00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:16.880
a less crazy place,

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:19.563
something that feels
more settled and calm,

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:25.210
what do you do when life and
kids and the natural layers

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:27.596
of things come back in?

00:24:27.596 --> 00:24:30.679
- (foreign language)

00:24:42.270 --> 00:24:43.930
- With children, it's really easy

00:24:43.930 --> 00:24:47.700
to accumulate a lot of items and clutter.

00:24:47.700 --> 00:24:50.370
But in those instances,
I work with the children

00:24:50.370 --> 00:24:52.300
to talk to them and hey, what sparks joy,

00:24:52.300 --> 00:24:53.133
what makes you happy?

00:24:53.133 --> 00:24:56.140
And I have them play and
then you integrate them

00:24:56.140 --> 00:24:57.806
into the process.

00:24:57.806 --> 00:25:00.680
- Oh.
(audience laughs)

00:25:00.680 --> 00:25:03.590
Oh yeah, no, I wasn't doing that.

00:25:03.590 --> 00:25:06.160
So now I should go with my children

00:25:06.160 --> 00:25:08.580
and take them through their things

00:25:08.580 --> 00:25:11.200
and figure out what sparks joy for them.

00:25:11.200 --> 00:25:16.200
And then we can prioritize
what we should keep

00:25:17.450 --> 00:25:18.770
and what we should let go of.

00:25:18.770 --> 00:25:20.423
Is that the right advice?

00:25:21.320 --> 00:25:24.403
- (foreign language)

00:25:31.521 --> 00:25:33.810
- Absolutely, talk about
this with your kids.

00:25:33.810 --> 00:25:36.080
And it's very important
that at a young age

00:25:36.080 --> 00:25:38.550
they understand what it means to spark joy

00:25:38.550 --> 00:25:40.300
and what sparks joy to them.

00:25:40.300 --> 00:25:43.040
- You have a new online tidying course.

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:44.930
Will you please tell us about that

00:25:44.930 --> 00:25:46.903
so we can all watch it and learn?

00:25:48.374 --> 00:25:51.457
- (foreign language)

00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:06.890
- Absolutely, so what
this is is a visual guide

00:26:06.890 --> 00:26:08.610
to the tidying process.

00:26:08.610 --> 00:26:10.220
And of course, if you read the book,

00:26:10.220 --> 00:26:12.920
some people can visualize
it, but this really helps

00:26:12.920 --> 00:26:16.240
because it is a very visual
medium to see the process,

00:26:16.240 --> 00:26:18.890
how it gets done and help people go

00:26:18.890 --> 00:26:21.670
through the entire process of tidying up.

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:25.580
- Last week, I was mesmerized
by how you fold underwear.

00:26:25.580 --> 00:26:30.580
The underwear you chose were very petite

00:26:30.950 --> 00:26:32.980
and I tend to wear something

00:26:32.980 --> 00:26:35.808
that looks more like a parachute.

00:26:35.808 --> 00:26:38.030
(audience laughs)

00:26:38.030 --> 00:26:41.770
Like, if there's a fire, we
should all grab my underwear

00:26:41.770 --> 00:26:43.841
and use it.

00:26:43.841 --> 00:26:44.674
(audience laughs)

00:26:44.674 --> 00:26:49.390
How would you fold a fitted
sheet or my underwear?

00:26:50.327 --> 00:26:52.599
(audience laughs)

00:26:52.599 --> 00:26:55.824
- [Marie] (foreign language)

00:26:55.824 --> 00:26:58.120
- [Interpreter] So you wanna
take the most important bits

00:26:58.120 --> 00:27:02.491
and fold it to the top like so, inward.

00:27:02.491 --> 00:27:06.241
- [Marie] (foreign language)

00:27:08.546 --> 00:27:10.193
- [Interpreter] Oh, you
could fold it in half.

00:27:11.593 --> 00:27:13.897
- [Marie] (foreign language)

00:27:13.897 --> 00:27:16.800
- Because this is cotton and
it's a very rigid fabric,

00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:19.043
you don't have to fold it as many times.

00:27:20.777 --> 00:27:22.712
- [Marie] (foreign language)
- [Interpreter] Perfect!

00:27:22.712 --> 00:27:24.950
(audience applauds)
- I appreciate you so much.

00:27:24.950 --> 00:27:29.460
What you've put into the world,
you've helped and allowed

00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:34.460
and normalized us asking what
joy is and how we find it.

00:27:36.300 --> 00:27:39.050
I think I'm gonna have to pinch myself.

00:27:39.050 --> 00:27:41.570
I just wanna say, Marie, that

00:27:44.165 --> 00:27:47.720
I truly hope to make you proud.

00:27:53.053 --> 00:27:55.560
I have your picture on my desk

00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:59.199
and I hope that I haven't scared you away.

00:27:59.199 --> 00:28:00.153
(audience laughs)

00:28:00.153 --> 00:28:03.822
- (foreign language)

00:28:03.822 --> 00:28:04.900
- I am ecstatic right now.

00:28:04.900 --> 00:28:07.030
Let's go spread more joy around the world.

00:28:07.030 --> 00:28:07.863
- Yes!

00:28:09.640 --> 00:28:11.460
Marie, I love you.

00:28:11.460 --> 00:28:13.960
You have changed my life.

00:28:13.960 --> 00:28:17.310
I look at everything now
just in a different way

00:28:17.310 --> 00:28:18.950
because of you.

00:28:18.950 --> 00:28:22.867
And we'll be right back with
more memories from season one.

00:28:23.822 --> 00:28:26.405
(upbeat music)

00:28:30.713 --> 00:28:34.030
(upbeat music)

00:28:34.030 --> 00:28:34.930
Welcome back.

00:28:34.930 --> 00:28:37.580
We're watching some
memorable season one moments

00:28:37.580 --> 00:28:40.560
and sharing behind the scene tidbits,

00:28:40.560 --> 00:28:43.400
some stuff you didn't see onscreen.

00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:46.070
It's a little season two pre-party.

00:28:46.070 --> 00:28:49.810
Of all the amazing guests we
welcomed during season one,

00:28:49.810 --> 00:28:53.000
this big, tall and handsome guy

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:55.680
was one of my very favorites.

00:28:55.680 --> 00:28:59.670
I like to think we really
are birds of a feather.

00:28:59.670 --> 00:29:01.490
And he even came dressed

00:29:01.490 --> 00:29:04.380
in the show's signature yellow color.

00:29:04.380 --> 00:29:09.380
It's the one, the only, my
lifelong love, Big Bird.

00:29:09.810 --> 00:29:13.650
He joined us to celebrate
World Kindness Day.

00:29:13.650 --> 00:29:15.390
Watch this.

00:29:15.390 --> 00:29:17.630
How is your morning so far?

00:29:17.630 --> 00:29:19.989
Always early, Bird?

00:29:19.989 --> 00:29:20.822
(Big Bird laughs)

00:29:20.822 --> 00:29:23.780
- Well, my day is going
great here on Sesame Street.

00:29:23.780 --> 00:29:25.230
And you know the old saying,

00:29:25.230 --> 00:29:27.864
the early bird gets the bird seed.

00:29:27.864 --> 00:29:29.479
(audience laughs)
(Big Bird laughs)

00:29:29.479 --> 00:29:31.290
(Drew laughs)

00:29:31.290 --> 00:29:32.280
- Yes, it does.

00:29:32.280 --> 00:29:34.830
I'm tongue tied 'cause I'm
so excited to be meet you.

00:29:34.830 --> 00:29:36.960
- Well, I'm excited to meet you.

00:29:36.960 --> 00:29:38.690
- It's a dream come true

00:29:38.690 --> 00:29:42.500
and today is World Kindness Day.

00:29:42.500 --> 00:29:46.550
Do you mind explaining
what it's all about?

00:29:46.550 --> 00:29:50.260
- Oh sure, well, I could tell
you what kindness is about.

00:29:50.260 --> 00:29:55.260
Kindness is about showing
people how much you care.

00:29:55.658 --> 00:30:00.658
And you can be kind to animals
and the environment too

00:30:01.050 --> 00:30:03.640
and it makes my friends feel good

00:30:03.640 --> 00:30:04.890
when I'm kind to them.

00:30:04.890 --> 00:30:08.460
So that makes me feel good, you know?

00:30:08.460 --> 00:30:10.986
- Yes, it's true.

00:30:10.986 --> 00:30:14.900
It's funny, the nicer you are to people,

00:30:14.900 --> 00:30:18.040
strangely, the better you feel yourself,

00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:20.500
but how do you show
kindness to your friends

00:30:20.500 --> 00:30:22.560
on Sesame Street?

00:30:22.560 --> 00:30:27.560
- Whenever I'm sad, my best
friend, Snuffy, he calls me

00:30:27.750 --> 00:30:29.390
and he cheers me up.

00:30:29.390 --> 00:30:31.090
And that's really kind.

00:30:31.090 --> 00:30:34.370
And also Grover, he always holds the door

00:30:34.370 --> 00:30:36.450
when he sees someone
leaving Hooper's Store

00:30:36.450 --> 00:30:39.565
with a lot of groceries,
so that's really kind.

00:30:39.565 --> 00:30:42.300
And Abby Cadabby, she's kind to the earth

00:30:42.300 --> 00:30:45.500
by watering the plants in her
garden and that's really kind.

00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:47.270
And you know what, Drew?

00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:49.640
Even Oscar the Grouch can be kind.

00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:52.857
He takes really good care
of his pet worm, Slimey.

00:30:52.857 --> 00:30:56.040
- Well, in honor of World
Kindness Day, we wanted

00:30:56.040 --> 00:31:00.450
to do a little sketch we're
calling Kind Tweets, get it?

00:31:00.450 --> 00:31:02.262
Tweet, tweet.
(Big Bird laughs)

00:31:02.262 --> 00:31:03.720
(birds chirp)

00:31:03.720 --> 00:31:04.840
- You know what, Drew?

00:31:04.840 --> 00:31:07.309
I'm really great at tweeting.

00:31:07.309 --> 00:31:08.510
(Drew laughs)

00:31:08.510 --> 00:31:10.560
Yeah, I tweet all the time.

00:31:10.560 --> 00:31:12.350
Tweet tweet, tweet tweet, see?
(audience laughs)

00:31:12.350 --> 00:31:15.540
- I would love to follow you on Tweeter.

00:31:15.540 --> 00:31:19.130
Well, we're gonna read the
kindest tweets that we found

00:31:19.130 --> 00:31:22.690
on the internet to spread
a little happiness today.

00:31:22.690 --> 00:31:24.560
Big Bird, are you ready?

00:31:24.560 --> 00:31:26.000
- Oh sure, I'm ready, Drew.

00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:27.843
- Okay, I'm gonna go first.

00:31:28.762 --> 00:31:33.270
@dadof5 tweeted, #hero,

00:31:33.270 --> 00:31:35.710
when nine-year-old Reese lost her home

00:31:35.710 --> 00:31:38.300
in California's biggest wildfire,

00:31:38.300 --> 00:31:42.130
she also lost her baseball
cards, 100 of them.

00:31:42.130 --> 00:31:43.640
And she was heartbroken.

00:31:43.640 --> 00:31:47.070
And when Kevin Ashford, a
lifelong collector found out,

00:31:47.070 --> 00:31:48.460
he knew what he had to do.

00:31:48.460 --> 00:31:52.192
He gave her all 25,000 of his own cards.

00:31:52.192 --> 00:31:54.208
(audience applauds)

00:31:54.208 --> 00:31:55.208
- Wow!
- Wow!

00:31:57.770 --> 00:31:58.820
Oh, I love this.

00:31:58.820 --> 00:32:02.530
Okay, Big Bird, tweet tweet, you're next.

00:32:02.530 --> 00:32:03.900
- Okay, here we go.

00:32:03.900 --> 00:32:06.324
This one is from my friend, Ernie.

00:32:06.324 --> 00:32:07.157
(audience applauds)

00:32:07.157 --> 00:32:10.230
And it says for World Kindness Day,

00:32:10.230 --> 00:32:14.350
my old buddy Bert gave me
his favorite argyle socks

00:32:14.350 --> 00:32:16.569
to make some new sock puppets.

00:32:16.569 --> 00:32:17.720
(audience laughs)
(Big Bird laughs)

00:32:17.720 --> 00:32:20.868
Gee, Bert, that was really
kind of you, it says.

00:32:20.868 --> 00:32:22.030
(Big Bird laughs)
He's right.

00:32:22.030 --> 00:32:23.170
- Okay, that was so kind.

00:32:23.170 --> 00:32:25.177
Okay, one more tweet tweet.

00:32:25.177 --> 00:32:28.930
@thegoodnewsnetwork
tweets seven-year-old boy

00:32:28.930 --> 00:32:32.420
who was bullied opens a huge food pantry,

00:32:32.420 --> 00:32:35.450
making his life all about positive energy.

00:32:35.450 --> 00:32:36.610
I love this.

00:32:36.610 --> 00:32:38.930
Cavanaugh Bell told his mom he wanted

00:32:38.930 --> 00:32:42.940
to start a GoFundMe page
to fulfill his mission

00:32:42.940 --> 00:32:45.970
of assembling and distributing
care packages filled

00:32:45.970 --> 00:32:50.040
with food and toiletries
for his elderly neighbors.

00:32:50.040 --> 00:32:51.270
And guess what?

00:32:51.270 --> 00:32:53.940
Cavanaugh is here now,

00:32:53.940 --> 00:32:55.203
hello.
- Really?

00:32:56.521 --> 00:32:58.356
- Hi.
(audience applauds)

00:32:58.356 --> 00:33:00.380
- Hello, Cavanaugh.

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:04.530
What an amazingly kind person you are.

00:33:04.530 --> 00:33:08.916
What motivates your kindness
and positive attitude?

00:33:08.916 --> 00:33:10.700
- Well, I know we're all going

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:15.140
through some hard times right
now and I just wanna make sure

00:33:15.140 --> 00:33:19.347
that people know that people feel happy

00:33:19.347 --> 00:33:21.010
and that they're loved.

00:33:21.010 --> 00:33:25.070
So every day, I think of
how I can make this world

00:33:25.070 --> 00:33:30.070
a better place, whether it's
by my care packs or speaking up

00:33:30.670 --> 00:33:32.690
and speaking out against bullying.

00:33:32.690 --> 00:33:36.903
I wanna show the world that
being positive is cool.

00:33:36.903 --> 00:33:40.556
(audience applauds)
- Yeah.

00:33:40.556 --> 00:33:42.263
Oh, Cavanaugh, I love what you said there.

00:33:42.263 --> 00:33:43.783
It's so so special.

00:33:44.710 --> 00:33:49.320
How does it feel to help out
so many of your neighbors?

00:33:49.320 --> 00:33:51.800
- It makes me feel so beautiful inside

00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:56.800
that I get to have people
have what they need.

00:33:56.960 --> 00:34:00.756
And my goal was to help
1,000 people in my community,

00:34:00.756 --> 00:34:03.720
but I've helped over 10,000 people,

00:34:03.720 --> 00:34:06.482
not in just my community
but all over the country.

00:34:06.482 --> 00:34:08.028
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

00:34:08.028 --> 00:34:08.861
- Wow!
- Wow!

00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:12.980
And Cavanaugh, how have
the people responded

00:34:12.980 --> 00:34:15.373
to your amazing work?

00:34:16.670 --> 00:34:20.820
- Well, they're usually kind of surprised

00:34:20.820 --> 00:34:23.240
and sometimes they cry happy tears

00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:27.330
because no one has
helped them like I have.

00:34:27.330 --> 00:34:31.560
But the most awesome part is
I've been able to inspire kids

00:34:31.560 --> 00:34:34.990
to help their community,
like Charlie, my friend.

00:34:34.990 --> 00:34:38.030
He's in New Jersey, he's
helping his community.

00:34:38.030 --> 00:34:42.640
And Nicholas, my other
friend, he is in Atlanta,

00:34:42.640 --> 00:34:45.860
or you could say Georgia,
helping his community.

00:34:45.860 --> 00:34:46.693
(audience applauds)

00:34:46.693 --> 00:34:49.210
- We are all so impressed
with you, Cavanaugh.

00:34:49.210 --> 00:34:51.490
And our friends at Sprouts

00:34:51.490 --> 00:34:55.610
and the Sprouts Healthy
Communities Foundation heard

00:34:55.610 --> 00:34:59.180
about what you're doing and
would like to help you continue

00:34:59.180 --> 00:35:04.180
to spread kindness by giving
you $10,000 in healthy food.

00:35:04.444 --> 00:35:07.910
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

00:35:07.910 --> 00:35:09.630
- Thank you so much.

00:35:09.630 --> 00:35:11.263
- Wait, look, Cavanaugh.

00:35:12.570 --> 00:35:13.403
Here we go.

00:35:14.649 --> 00:35:17.433
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

00:35:17.433 --> 00:35:20.766
- And Sprouts is such a wonderful market

00:35:22.160 --> 00:35:25.270
with such incredible
produce and healthy food

00:35:25.270 --> 00:35:30.270
and beautiful quality
companies that they sell.

00:35:30.570 --> 00:35:32.360
Oh, I just love them so much.

00:35:32.360 --> 00:35:35.820
And I was so thrilled that
they stepped up to the plate

00:35:35.820 --> 00:35:38.640
in the way that they
did, all inspired by you.

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:40.476
Thank you, Cavanaugh.

00:35:40.476 --> 00:35:41.309
(audience applauds)

00:35:41.309 --> 00:35:42.590
Thank you so much.

00:35:42.590 --> 00:35:45.760
I was truly star struck by Big Bird.

00:35:45.760 --> 00:35:48.100
I mean, who wouldn't be?

00:35:48.100 --> 00:35:49.694
We'll be right back.

00:35:49.694 --> 00:35:52.277
(upbeat music)

00:35:55.712 --> 00:35:57.480
(upbeat music)

00:35:57.480 --> 00:35:58.570
Welcome back.

00:35:58.570 --> 00:36:02.060
It's time to surprise Alicia
and her sister, Tiffany.

00:36:02.060 --> 00:36:04.120
Throughout the hour,
they've been getting a tour

00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:06.440
of our building and are
about to enter the studio.

00:36:06.440 --> 00:36:09.720
And we have to be quiet
because they have no idea

00:36:09.720 --> 00:36:10.670
that we're filming.

00:36:14.930 --> 00:36:16.017
- Oh wow!
- Hi.

00:36:18.777 --> 00:36:20.388
- Oh!
(sisters laugh)

00:36:20.388 --> 00:36:21.221
- Hi!

00:36:22.554 --> 00:36:23.751
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:36:23.751 --> 00:36:25.810
- Hi, Alicia and Tiffany.

00:36:25.810 --> 00:36:26.810
- Oh my God!

00:36:28.391 --> 00:36:29.224
Oh my God!

00:36:30.077 --> 00:36:32.156
- And guess what, you're on camera too.

00:36:32.156 --> 00:36:33.156
- Oh my God!

00:36:34.362 --> 00:36:36.950
- It's so nice to meet you.

00:36:36.950 --> 00:36:41.110
- Oh my goodness, I
cannot believe we're here.

00:36:41.110 --> 00:36:43.743
- I'm so excited to meet both of you.

00:36:43.743 --> 00:36:47.350
I just love what you're
doing in the world.

00:36:47.350 --> 00:36:49.610
By the way, I'm obsessed
with your logo too.

00:36:49.610 --> 00:36:51.880
I'm a nut for graphics.

00:36:51.880 --> 00:36:52.713
- [Tiffany] She made it herself.

00:36:52.713 --> 00:36:53.550
- Yeah, I made it myself.

00:36:53.550 --> 00:36:56.380
Yes, I made the logo myself
and we're obsessed with you,

00:36:56.380 --> 00:36:58.870
everything flower and your love

00:36:58.870 --> 00:37:00.710
for the environment and everything.

00:37:00.710 --> 00:37:02.460
- Our favorite movie is "Ever After".

00:37:02.460 --> 00:37:05.320
- Yeah, so we are just so obsessed.

00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:07.880
- Well, and sisters is
my entire universe now

00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:09.440
because I have two daughters.

00:37:09.440 --> 00:37:12.380
So it rules every move I make.

00:37:12.380 --> 00:37:17.080
And I loved reading about
how is it true you walked off

00:37:17.080 --> 00:37:21.430
a subway and saw this space and
something, a light went off?

00:37:21.430 --> 00:37:23.740
- Yes, I was traveling with my sister.

00:37:23.740 --> 00:37:24.870
We were coming back home.

00:37:24.870 --> 00:37:26.890
And so there was this environmental space

00:37:26.890 --> 00:37:29.560
in our neighborhood where weeds
were up to everyone's waist

00:37:29.560 --> 00:37:30.620
and there was trash

00:37:30.620 --> 00:37:32.560
and people were using
it as a dumping ground.

00:37:32.560 --> 00:37:35.410
And so I decided that I wanted
to do something about it

00:37:35.410 --> 00:37:36.840
and improve that environmental space

00:37:36.840 --> 00:37:38.300
so that the community could use it

00:37:38.300 --> 00:37:41.430
for access to transportation, gardening.

00:37:41.430 --> 00:37:43.850
And so that started my organization.

00:37:43.850 --> 00:37:46.540
- And I mean, I really
wanna learn from you

00:37:46.540 --> 00:37:48.300
because I feel like

00:37:51.640 --> 00:37:54.760
sometimes we look at things
that we would like to change,

00:37:54.760 --> 00:37:58.460
but you actually went ahead,
figured it out, changed it

00:37:58.460 --> 00:38:01.420
and then continued the
work on and on and on.

00:38:01.420 --> 00:38:05.640
So I mean, I feel like we
have a lot to learn from you.

00:38:05.640 --> 00:38:07.900
- Thank you so much.

00:38:07.900 --> 00:38:10.610
I mean, the only thing I
could say is everything starts

00:38:10.610 --> 00:38:11.720
with one small step.

00:38:11.720 --> 00:38:14.140
Sometimes we don't think that
one small action will have

00:38:14.140 --> 00:38:16.970
a ripple effect, but doing
one small thing like helping

00:38:16.970 --> 00:38:19.330
a neighbor or helping clean
up environmental space

00:38:19.330 --> 00:38:20.470
can help improve communities

00:38:20.470 --> 00:38:23.710
and help improve our environment,
so just one small thing

00:38:23.710 --> 00:38:24.850
at a time, I guess.

00:38:24.850 --> 00:38:27.170
- So you did that and then you kept going

00:38:27.170 --> 00:38:28.850
and you've done more spaces, right?

00:38:28.850 --> 00:38:31.260
- Mm-hm, so I do spaces
throughout New York City

00:38:31.260 --> 00:38:34.110
in every borough and I connect
with other community leaders

00:38:34.110 --> 00:38:34.943
or people who are like,

00:38:34.943 --> 00:38:37.160
"Hey, I have an environmental
project, I need help."

00:38:37.160 --> 00:38:40.770
So I give them tools, resources,
help them with everything

00:38:40.770 --> 00:38:43.500
that I wish that I had
help with starting out.

00:38:43.500 --> 00:38:46.740
- And now that field that
you walked out of that subway

00:38:46.740 --> 00:38:49.930
that day and had the light bulb
go off, what is it like now?

00:38:49.930 --> 00:38:52.400
- So now, it's a commuter path there.

00:38:52.400 --> 00:38:54.060
So it connects all the neighborhoods

00:38:54.060 --> 00:38:55.440
with access to the train.

00:38:55.440 --> 00:38:57.930
So it's no longer a dirt
path, it's no longer weeds

00:38:57.930 --> 00:39:01.030
to the hip and people could
get to garden and go out

00:39:01.030 --> 00:39:02.100
and enjoy the space.

00:39:02.100 --> 00:39:03.520
Young people get to play there.

00:39:03.520 --> 00:39:05.713
So it's a beautiful space now.

00:39:06.810 --> 00:39:08.210
- I'm so impressed with you.

00:39:09.230 --> 00:39:11.820
I mean, are you guys close?

00:39:11.820 --> 00:39:13.250
You look so much alike,

00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:14.990
I totally get that you're sisters.

00:39:14.990 --> 00:39:16.150
- So we're very close.

00:39:16.150 --> 00:39:18.600
We live together.
- We live together.

00:39:18.600 --> 00:39:20.050
Yes, and so we're
obsessed with you as well

00:39:20.050 --> 00:39:21.050
because we bought our first home

00:39:21.050 --> 00:39:23.610
and we renovated the whole
thing ourselves, yeah.

00:39:23.610 --> 00:39:25.304
And we picked out paint colors,

00:39:25.304 --> 00:39:26.770
- Furniture, everything.
Everything, yeah.

